description:
Implement a 4-bit binary multiplier. The module takes two 4-bit inputs, A and B, and produces an 8-bit output representing their product. The multiplication is performed using a shift-and-add algorithm, where each bit of A is evaluated, and if it is set to 1, the corresponding shifted version of B is added to the product. This design effectively captures the fundamental operation of binary multiplication in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [7:0] product
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [7:0] product
);reg [3:0] shifted_B;
reg [3:0] i;

always @ (A or B) begin
    product <= 0;
    shifted_B <= B;
    for (i = 0; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
        if (A[i] == 1) begin
            product <= product + (shifted_B << i);
        end
    end
end

endmodule

